uiautomationcore: navigate to a *matching* sibling or child instead of giving up with E_NOTIMPL

Symptom and who hits it.  The .NET UI Automation client asks its own provider (and Wine's) to
walk the element tree with a condition.  Wine's `conditional_navigate_uia_node()`
(dlls/uiautomationcore/uia_client.c) handled `NavigateDirection_Parent` with a condition but for
NextSibling/PreviousSibling/FirstChild/LastChild it did:

    if (cond->ConditionType != ConditionType_True)
    {
        FIXME("ConditionType %d based navigation for dir %d is not implemented.\n", ...);
        return E_NOTIMPL;
    }

`System.Windows.Automation.TreeWalker` does not pass `Condition.TrueCondition`: both
`TreeWalker.ControlViewWalker` and `TreeWalker.RawViewWalker` build a **`Not`** condition
(ConditionType_Not == 5) to exclude invisible elements, so every `GetFirstChild`,
`GetNextSibling`, `GetPreviousSibling` and `GetParent` through the managed tree walker hit that
branch.  Measured with tools/winapi/uiaprobe.cs, which calls exactly those APIs under Wine:

    $ wine C:\uiaprobe.exe
    FromHandle ok: uiaprobeTarget
    0a48:fixme:uiautomationcore:conditional_navigate_uia_node ConditionType 5 based navigation for dir 1 is not implemented.
    automation threw: NotImplementedException: The method or operation is not implemented.

so the managed caller got a *hard* failure where Windows returns the first matching element.  This
is the same API family as the `DwmGetWindowAttribute` line Solid Edge's own log shows when the
sketch will not close, which is why it was chased: `UIAutomationClient`'s `IsWindowReallyVisible`
both asks DWM about `DWMWA_CLOAKED` and walks the tree through these calls.

The Windows behaviour restored.  `Navigate` with a condition returns the first element in the
requested direction that satisfies the condition (`FirstChild`/`LastChild`: the first/last
matching child; `NextSibling`/`PreviousSibling`: the first matching sibling in that direction).
The patch walks in the direction until a node matches, transferring ownership the same way the
existing `NavigateDirection_Parent` loop does.

Verification.  After the patch the probe's tree walk completes instead of throwing
(tools/winapi/uiaprobe.cs, run under this fork), and the module's own suite is unchanged:
`tools/run_wine_tests.sh uiautomationcore`.  No new unit test is shipped with this patch: the
suite's existing navigation test drives every call through a per-test method-sequence expectation
(`ok_method_sequence`), and inserting calls there would rewrite that expectation rather than test
the new behaviour; the end-to-end probe above is the evidence instead.
--- a/dlls/uiautomationcore/uia_client.c	2026-09-18 15:36:23.000000000 -0500
+++ b/dlls/uiautomationcore/uia_client.c	2026-10-01 05:50:06.293715480 -0500
@@ -999,6 +999,49 @@
     return S_OK;
 }
 
+/* Walk from `start` in `nav_dir` until a node matching `cond` is reached.  `start` is borrowed;
+ * any node acquired on the way is released.  Windows returns the first *matching* element in
+ * that direction, which is what .NET's TreeWalker needs: TreeWalker's view conditions are `Not`
+ * conditions (ConditionType_Not), so every GetNextSibling/GetFirstChild call arrives here with a
+ * condition that is not ConditionType_True. */
+static HRESULT conditional_navigate_siblings(struct uia_node *start, int nav_dir,
+        struct UiaCondition *cond, HUIANODE *out_node)
+{
+    struct uia_node *cur = start;
+    BOOL owned = FALSE;
+    HRESULT hr;
+
+    *out_node = NULL;
+    while (1)
+    {
+        HUIANODE next = NULL;
+
+        hr = navigate_uia_node(cur, nav_dir, &next);
+        if (FAILED(hr)) return hr;
+        if (!next) break;
+
+        if (owned) IWineUiaNode_Release(&cur->IWineUiaNode_iface);
+        cur = unsafe_impl_from_IWineUiaNode((IWineUiaNode *)next);
+        owned = TRUE;
+
+        if (cond->ConditionType == ConditionType_True)
+        {
+            *out_node = next;
+            return S_OK;
+        }
+        hr = uia_condition_check(next, cond);
+        if (FAILED(hr)) return hr;
+        if (uia_condition_matched(hr))
+        {
+            *out_node = next;
+            return S_OK;
+        }
+    }
+
+    if (owned) IWineUiaNode_Release(&cur->IWineUiaNode_iface);
+    return S_OK;
+}
+
 static HRESULT conditional_navigate_uia_node(struct uia_node *node, int nav_dir, struct UiaCondition *cond,
         HUIANODE *out_node)
 {
@@ -1039,17 +1082,45 @@
         break;
     }
 
-    case NavigateDirection_NextSibling:
-    case NavigateDirection_PreviousSibling:
     case NavigateDirection_FirstChild:
